g tests and supporting source intact.\n\nIn Doc/library/urllib.parse.rst, add a focused explanation and executable examples of the observed boundary/error behavior, including the distinction between constructing the parsed result and accessing its port. Preserve existing documentation. New examples must be self-contained together (include their imports), use >>> prompts, and show their real outputs or exceptions. Do not copy an untested expectation into the explanation as if saving it established library behavior.\n\nThe host runs the tests scope after each accepted test-file edit, and the public scope after each accepted documentation edit. Tests scope runs the saved and edited suite, observes the required API/input paths, and checks that the new tests detect changes to exception class/arguments/message, validation timing and valid boundary values. Examples scope executes the newly added examples. Public includes both scopes and preservation checks. All scopes are available on request. Only a public pass on the current candidate authorizes submission. Documentation prose also receives a separate review after the run.\n\nStart from the supplied saved files, find the relevant source, complete both contributions, use actual feedback, and submit the checked result. Provisional work is permitted; preserve consequential unresolved questions in the optional working account and revise them when evidence changes. A saved expectation is authored work, not an execution observation. This task describes a new contribution in the current session, not a report that a previous session's edit has failed.\n","verification":{"after_accepted_edit":{"Doc/library/urllib.parse.rst":"public","Lib/test/test_urlparse.py":"tests"},"checks":{"examples":null,"public":null,"tests":null},"outstanding":[],"submission":{"eligible":false,"scope":"public"}},"visibility":{"capacity_omitted_inspections":false,"recovery_inspections_retained":0,"retained_inventory":{"accepted":true,"entries":[{"end_line